    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 83.29. Facing Elder, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong park factor and a favorable matchup that boosts his power potential in the #3 hole. Other high-ceiling plays include **Drake Baldwin** (72.68) and **Jacob Wilson** (70.28). Both are hitting leadoff against exploitable starters with xERAs above 4.50; for **Drake Baldwin**, a 0.387 xwOBA combined with a neutral platoon advantage makes him a prime candidate for runs scored. Additionally, **Heliot Ramos** (68.01) is a primary start, as the wind blowing out at his venue provides a crucial lift to his raw projection, offsetting a slightly unfavorable park factor.\n\nThe decision to bench **Kyle Tucker** (51.31) remains our most difficult call today. While **Kyle Tucker** is an elite talent, his scoring efficiency is suppressed by an unfavorable matchup against McLean, who carries a stingy 3.43 xERA, and a lower-than-usual batting order position that limits his RBI opportunities. In comparison, **Curtis Mead** (57.04) and **Jackson Merrill** (59.99) were prioritized for their high-leverage spots in the lineup and superior platoon alignments. We are keeping a close watch on **Jackson Merrill**, as his matchup against P\u00e9rez offers a unique opportunity for stolen bases due to the pitcher's slow delivery, a key metric for our roster construction given our emphasis on speed.\n\nWhile we are confident in this configuration, risk remains. Both **Nasim Nunez** (61.57) and **Curtis Mead** are facing a challenging arm in Bratt, who, despite an elevated xERA, requires careful monitoring of pitch efficiency. We have also factored in the lack of official lineup confirmation for some players, assuming historical batting positions; should any of these players drop lower in their respective orders, we may see their efficiency scores shift downward before first pitch. We continue to prioritize consistent plate appearances, ensuring that our roster depth\u2014including the likes of **Brayan Rocchio**, **Denzer Guzman**, and **Luis Lara**\u2014is ready if any of our starters face late-scratch conditions.",
